# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example  —  TEMPLATE OF REQUIRED ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# It documents every environment variable the app needs in order to run,
# WITHOUT containing any real values. It is safe to commit. The real `.env`
# is git-ignored and never leaves a developer's machine.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in the real values for your machine.
#
# IMPORTANT — THE "EXPO_PUBLIC_" PREFIX
# Expo only exposes variables to app code when they start with EXPO_PUBLIC_.
# That prefix also means the value is BAKED INTO THE JS BUNDLE and is readable
# by anyone who inspects the app. Never put a secret here — no API keys, no
# signing secrets. Only non-sensitive configuration like a base URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the EGKMS backend, including the /api/v1 version prefix.
#
# NOTE FOR MOBILE: "localhost" refers to the PHONE, not your computer. On a
# physical device you must use your machine's LAN IP address, e.g.
#   http://192.168.1.42:5000/api/v1
# Android emulator maps the host machine to 10.0.2.2:
#   http://10.0.2.2:5000/api/v1
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1
